---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/paths';
import { APP, MANUAL } from '../../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Manual — ipnx"
  description="How to use ipnx: first launch, the terminals, the DMD 5620 and mux, sharing folders with your Mac, networking, settings and troubleshooting."
  eyebrow="Documentation"
  heading="Manual"
  intro="Eight sections. Enough to be at home on a machine from 1985 without having been there the first time."
>
  <div class="py-8">
    {/*
      The manual-page header, used once and here: NAME(section) on both
      margins with the title between. It is a reference rather than a costume —
      this app ships the Eighth Edition manual, and anyone who has read one
      will recognise the shape immediately.
    */}
    <div class="manpage-rule pb-1 text-[12px] tracking-[0.08em] text-muted uppercase">
      <span>IPNX(1)</span>
      <span class="hidden sm:inline">{APP.system}</span>
      <span>IPNX(1)</span>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 max-w-[68ch]">
      <h2 class="font-sans text-[12px] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-ink uppercase">Name</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[17px] text-body">
        ipnx — Research Unix Eighth Edition on an emulated VAX-11/780
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-7 font-sans text-[12px] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-ink uppercase">
        Description
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[17px] text-body">
        This manual covers the app: what it does on first launch, what the windows are, and how to
        get at the parts of the machine that are not obvious. It does not try to teach Unix — the
        system carries its own manual, and <code class="bg-chip px-1 font-mono text-[0.86em]"
          >man</code
        > works inside it exactly as it did.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-sans text-[12px] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-ink uppercase">
      Contents
    </h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 border-t border-rule">
      {
        MANUAL.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="border-b border-rule">
            <a
              href={href(`/manual/${s.slug}`)}
              class="group grid gap-x-5 gap-y-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,22rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:items-baseline"
            >
              <span class="font-mono text-[13px] text-muted">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <span class="font-serif text-[20px] font-bold text-ink group-hover:text-emphasis">
                {s.title}
              </span>
              <span class="text-[15px] text-muted">{s.blurb}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="mt-10 text-[15px] text-muted">
      Something missing or wrong? <a
        href={href('/support')}
        class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emphasis">Tell me</a
      > — the manual is as much a part of this as the code.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
